-- title:
--   Igusa bound: [SL₂(ℤ):±Γ_{H_1}]≤[T:L(j(x))]
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell_g \ge 3$ dividing $M'$; let $H_1 \le (\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ be the intersection of the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$ with the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is an algebra over a commutative ring $A$. Assume three equivariance hypotheses over arbitrary $A$-algebras $T$: that a variable change $C$ carries a $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point $D$ of $W$ (so $(x_P,y_P)$ lies on the affine equation of $W$, $(W.\mathrm{pre}\Psi\,\ell_g)(x_P)=0$, and $x_Q=x_P$, $y_Q=y_P$) to a $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point of $C \bullet W$; that it carries `IsGamma0PowAt` data for $p,k$ to `IsGamma0PowAt` data for the transported polynomial `kernelVariableChangeDeg C (gamma0PowDeg p k) h`; and that it preserves divisibility of `inLineMulPoly` in the corresponding transported form. Assume further a family of group laws $\mathcal G$ on the projective models which is chord–tangent and has the origin as identity, a level transport $\mathcal T$ for Drinfeld level-$q$ structures satisfying `IsSectionTransport`, and the existence, for every variable change and every coefficient change, of a graded ring homomorphism of projective-model rings satisfying `IsVariableChangeHom` respectively `IsCoefficientHom` and pulling back the irrelevant ideal as required. Let $T$ be a field which is an $L$-algebra and an $A$-algebra compatibly, and let $x$ be a $T$-point of the moduli datum attached to `rigidDataH1Pow A ℓg M' q …` — a variable-change class of a Weierstrass curve over $T$ with unit discriminant carrying a $\Gamma_0$-type family of kernel polynomials indexed by the prime factors of $M'$, a $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point, a Drinfeld basis of level $q$, and the linking condition `IsGamma1Link`. If $j(x)$ is transcendental over $L$ and $T$ is finite-dimensional over $L(j(x))$, then the index in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ of the subgroup generated by $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ (the image in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ of the preimage of $H_1$ under the lower-right-entry character of $\Gamma_0(q^2M')$) together with $-1$ is at most $\dim_{L(j(x))} T$.
--
--   This is the Igusa-type lower bound for the degree of a field over which an $H_1$-level structure with transcendental $j$-invariant can be defined: the field generated by such a structure over $L(j)$ is at least as large as the index of $\pm\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$, reflecting the fullness of the monodromy of level structures over the $j$-line. It feeds the density statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.dense_range_classify_of_jOf_eq_jqNModC_of_exists_ringHom_rigidDataH1Pow_of_finiteType`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.dense_range_classify_of_jOf_eq_jqNModC_of_exists_ringHom_rigidDataH1Pow_of_finiteType), where it converts a degree bound into surjectivity onto the relevant modular curve.
